Zeitgeist wrote:
> Soon enough, he came to a large castle with the drawbridge up.  He
> couldn't figure out how to get in, so he decided to busk with his
> bugle,
> to earn some extra zorkmids.  All of a sudden, the drawbridge came
> down and monsters started crossing the moat.
>
Bananas replayed the same tune, and the drawbridge closed again,
squashing the monster under the portcullis.  This looked like a fun
diversion from fighting all those monsters, so Bananas kept playing the

same tune over and over, until the first room was cleared.  Bananas
cleared the rest of the castle without much trouble and soon had a
spiffly new wand of prize of your choice.  He asked for 2 scrolls of
charging.  The powers that be must have misheard him though, as he was
only given one.

Bananas himself will tell the rest of the story (greatly abridged)

"I fell into the valley, and found a random monster with lev boots.  A
very timely find.  I used up the wished for marker and my original
marker, to make my AC -29.  I still want my protection back though.
Damn
gremlins."

"I dispatched Jubilex with a wand of digging.  Asmodeus was below him.

I fell through a trapdoor, then made my way up.  Asmodeus and his
cronies were beating me up, so I waited until he was next to me, then
went down the stairs."

"He followed and I stood on the upstair wacking him with vorpal blade
until he died.  His final action was to summon dispater (or whatever
his
name is), and I did the same to him. No bribes for you guys today.  I
also dispatched Baalzebub in much the same fashion.  I tamed two umber
hulks to help me clear a path between stairs in gehennom"

"I dispatched Vlad the impaler and collected the necessary loot from
his
tower.  He should really be called "Vlad the impotent", because he is
stupidly underpowered.  I found the vibrating square, marked it with a
ring of coins, and went back up to meet the wizard."

"I accidently woke the wizard while I was outside his tower.  He
teleported next to me and started hitting me.  I whacked him a few
times
with my staff to drain his level, then fired a wand of death at him
once
I was sure he was over dry land.  Since I hadn't expected to fight him
just yet, my candles were still in my stash on level 11.  I used a
cursed scroll of teleport to go to my stash, and grabbed the candles.
I
then used a second cursed teleport scroll to go to the gates of hell
and
a third to get down to the vibrating square level."

"I performed the ritual involving the bell, book and candles, then used

my final cursed scroll of teleport to go down one more level.  Imagine
my surprise when I ended up inside the sanctum!  I zapped a wand of
death at the priest, grabbed the amulet and quaffed a cursed potion of
gain level to get out of there without ever needing to see the
surrounding graveyard."

"I met Yeeenghu on the way up. That was a bummer.  Eventually beheaded
him though.  I love my vorpal blade.  The mysterious force was very
good
to me, only sending me back three times.  When I reached the quest
level, I thought I would show my old friend the amulet of yendor.  I
donned my jumping boots and started to jump towards his house.  However

I didn't realise that I was too tired to jump over some water and ended

up landing in it instead.  This blanked many of my scrolls and diluted
quite a few of my potions.  I decided that Hippocrates didn't need to
see the amulet that much and I could just keep going up."

"I got to level 1, checked my bag to make sure that my scrolls of gold
detection were still in there, but of course they had been blanked in
my
little 'swimming accident'.  I wasn't in the mood to play
'hotter/colder', so I wished up a new marker and wrote out the scrolls
I
needed.  The elemental planes didn't give me too much trouble, although

my wands of polymorph seemed strangely ineffective against air
elementals when I was engulfed in them." (Did this change in one of the

more recent releases?)

"Finally I got to the Astral plane.  This is what I had been training
for.  It was do or die.  Insert cliche here.  First I went right.
Famine got zapped with a wand of death and my wands of teleport cleared

a nice jumping path. Chaotic. Blast! I went back to the middle, saw
death up the centre, so I went to the left. I was stuck surrounded by
insects and archons and liches kept summoning more.  I eventually got
rid of the archon with vorpie, killed pestie with a wand of death and
started to struggle futher up and to the left.  I needed to break a
wand
of teleport before the area was clear enough to proceed. Two black
dragons helped me out by disintegrating some of the random monsters and

a cockatrice was nice enough to leave a corpse, and then things started

to move."

"I got stuck in the doorway, with pestilence behind me and someone with

a wand of lightning in front of me blinding me.  A few whacks with the
staff of misspelling, between quaffing healing potions, using the
unicorn horn and casting cure sickness and pestie went down. Several
statues later, I was at the altar. Neutral! I whistled in my pets
(charm
monster is a wonderful spell), chatted with the priest and offered the
amulet to my god."

"Huzzah!"


